ITEM I — Month Fill Verification and Monthly Rates
--------------------------------------------------
Monthly rainfall rates, missing days filled, and mm added per station:

1. Mahabaleshwar (5 valid seasons: 2016–2020; season mean daily rate = 52.30 mm/day):
   - Jun: rate = 26.77 mm/day | missing filled = 24 days total (4.80/yr) | mm added = 642.4 mm (128.5 mm/yr)
   - Jul: rate = 73.44 mm/day | missing filled = 16 days total (3.20/yr) | mm added = 1175.0 mm (235.0 mm/yr)
   - Aug: rate = 75.84 mm/day | missing filled = 12 days total (2.40/yr) | mm added = 910.1 mm (182.0 mm/yr)
   - Sep: rate = 27.97 mm/day | missing filled = 23 days total (4.60/yr) | mm added = 643.3 mm (128.7 mm/yr)

   Monthly Rate Comparison at Mahabaleshwar:
   - Jun (26.77 mm/day) and Sep (27.97 mm/day) are NOT within ~10% of Jul (73.44 mm/day) and Aug (75.84 mm/day).
     They are ~2.8x lower (a ~64% drop in daily intensity).
   - Cause of the seemingly modest shift (-0.066 on 3.855):
     The station's record is 87.7% complete (107.0 / 122 days present per season). Across 5 seasons, missing days
     average only 15.0 days/year across the entire season.
     - Uniform season fill added: 15.0 days * 52.30 mm/day = 784.5 mm/yr.
     - Month-specific fill added: 128.5 (Jun) + 235.0 (Jul) + 182.0 (Aug) + 128.7 (Sep) = 674.2 mm/yr.
     - Net gauge difference: 784.5 - 674.2 = 110.3 mm/yr.
     - Relative to total season precipitation (~6270 mm/yr), 110.3 mm is only 1.76% of total rainfall.
     - Scaled by CHIRPS denominator (1655 mm), delta_ratio = -110.3 / 1655 = -0.0666.
     Therefore, the shift is -0.066 because 88% of seasonal rainfall is fixed by direct observations,
     bounding the leverage of the fill adjustment.

